From 59c36b34b0855a61633f28d37dd4048b09538f2a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 13 Jul 2026 20:55:41 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 159/638] third_party: record AROS benchmark capabilities
 [chromium] [aros]

AI_PHASE: chromium-phase-4-ozone
AI_STATUS: checkpoint
ROOT_CAUSE: The windowed content_shell graph reached Google Benchmark and failed because its unknown-platform fallback requires rusage and libc gethostname contracts AROS does not provide.
FIX_REASON: Pin nested Google Benchmark commit 91f0065418, which models AROS explicitly and keeps unavailable metrics conservative rather than inventing POSIX support.
VALIDATION: Both failed Google Benchmark objects compile cleanly in out/aros-windowed.
RISK: Runtime benchmark CPU timing remains a wall-time approximation until AROS gains process and thread CPU accounting.
---
 third_party/google_benchmark/src | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/third_party/google_benchmark/src b/third_party/google_benchmark/src
index 344117638c..91f0065418 160000
--- a/third_party/google_benchmark/src
+++ b/third_party/google_benchmark/src
@@ -1 +1 @@
-Subproject commit 344117638c8ff7e239044fd0fa7085839fc03021
+Subproject commit 91f00654189b650378daa82ee981c5a9e2b52912
